# The single committed env TEMPLATE for the whole project — backend, frontend,
# and docker-compose all read the same set of keys. Make a real copy:
#
#   cp .env.example .env         # native `uv run ...` / `docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.yml` (prod)
#   cp .env.example .env.dev     # the dev stack: docker compose -f docker/docker-compose.dev.yml
#   cp .env.example .env.prod    # the prod stack's env_file
#
# `.env`, `.env.dev` and `.env.prod` are all git-ignored — never commit real
# secrets. backend/.env, apps/web/.env.local, and docker/.env are committed
# SYMLINKS to the root .env (see docker/README.md) — edit values here, not there.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  KEY NAMING — the KRUTRIM_AGENT_ prefix
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Backend settings (AppSettings, krutrim_agent_management/config.py) are read
#  with env_prefix="krutrim_agent_": pydantic strips that prefix and assigns to
#  the matching field, case-insensitively. So the field `vector_store_backend`
#  is set by KRUTRIM_AGENT_VECTOR_STORE_BACKEND, `qdrant_url` by
#  KRUTRIM_AGENT_QDRANT_URL, and so on — a BARE name (VECTOR_STORE_BACKEND) is
#  NOT picked up.
#
#  Exceptions that also accept a BARE name (handled explicitly in config.py):
#    * DEV_MODE            (as well as KRUTRIM_AGENT_DEV_MODE, which wins)
#    * REDIS_URL / REDIS_USER / REDIS_PASSWORD / REDIS_HOST / REDIS_PORT / ...
#    * LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY / LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY / LANGFUSE_BASE_URL / LANGFUSE_HOST
#
#  Not backend settings at all, always bare: OPENROUTER_*, TAVILY_*,
#  VITE_BACKEND_URL, TORCH_BACKEND, COMPOSE_*, QDRANT_HTTP_PORT/GRPC_PORT,
#  *_POLLING. The celery reaper uses its own KRUTRIM_AGENT_CELERY_ prefix.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compose (docker/docker-compose*.yml)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Both files use `name: ${COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME:-krutrim-agent[-dev]}` — override
# to run a fully isolated second copy of a stack (own containers/network/volumes).
# COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME=krutrim-agent
# Activates optional services. Set to `qdrant` to start the qdrant container
# (see the Vector store section below).
# COMPOSE_PROFILES=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LLM / embeddings provider
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Referenced by name from provider settings (harness/memory/settings.json,
# created on first run) and used directly for RAG embeddings (krutrim_agent_rag).
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_BASE_URL=
# Only when OPENROUTER_BASE_URL points at a local dev proxy that authenticates
# with its own master key — must match that proxy's LITELLM_MASTER_KEY.
# LITELLM_MASTER_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Web search — DuckDuckGo (default, zero-config) or Tavily
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# To enable Tavily (krutrim_agents_core/tools/websearch), set BOTH:
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_WEB_SEARCH_PROVIDER=tavily
# TAVILY_API_KEY=
# Optional — point tavily-python at a proxy / self-hosted gateway.
# TAVILY_SEARCH_API_BASE=https://api.tavily.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Backend — optional overrides (defaults shown). KRUTRIM_AGENT_ prefix.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_HOST=0.0.0.0
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_PORT=8000
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_SANDBOX_IMAGE=krutrim_agent-sandbox:latest
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_SANDBOX_RUNTIME=docker
# CORS: add the Vite dev-server origins when developing the frontend natively.
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_CORS_ORIGINS=["http://localhost:4200","http://localhost:5173"]
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_RAG_EMBEDDING_MODEL=qwen/qwen3-embedding-8b
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_RETRIEVAL_STRATEGY=vector_only
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_RAG_INJECTION_ENABLED=false
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_EDITION=community

# Celery broker/result-backend. The docker stacks set KRUTRIM_AGENT_REDIS_URL to
# the in-network `redis` service automatically; this value is for a backend run
# directly on the host against `docker compose ... up redis`.
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0

# Idle-container reaper tuning — note the KRUTRIM_AGENT_CELERY_ prefix.
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_CELERY_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=600
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_CELERY_BEAT_INTERVAL_SECONDS=60

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logging (krutrim_agent_management/logging_config.py) — shared by BOTH the
# FastAPI server and the Celery worker. Same knobs, different sink:
#   server -> $KRUTRIM_AGENT_LOG_DIR/server/server.log
#   worker -> $KRUTRIM_AGENT_LOG_DIR/worker/worker.log
# Defaults shown. stdlib logs (uvicorn/celery/httpx/...) are funnelled into
# the same files. When DEV_MODE is on, BOTH the console and file sinks drop
# to DEBUG regardless of the levels below (see .env.dev).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_LOG_DIR=~/.krutrim_agent/logs
# File-sink threshold. INFO keeps it lean; set DEBUG for the full step-by-step
# trace (RAG retrieval, chat turns, embedding stages, cleanup, ...).
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_LOG_LEVEL=INFO
# stderr threshold (console). Forced to DEBUG when DEV_MODE=true.
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_LOG_CONSOLE_LEVEL=INFO
# Rotation trigger — a period ("1 day"), a wall-clock time ("00:00"), or a
# size ("20 MB"). "1 day" = a fresh periodic log file every 24h.
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_LOG_ROTATION=1 day
# How long rotated files are kept before deletion.
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_LOG_RETENTION=14 days
# "" keeps rotated files plain; "zip"/"gz"/"tar.gz" compresses them.
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_LOG_COMPRESSION=
# Extended (variable-free) tracebacks in the file sink. Also on when DEV_MODE.
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_LOG_BACKTRACE=false
# Route stdlib logging through loguru so everything shares one format/file.
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_LOG_INTERCEPT_STD=true

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vector store (krutrim_agent_rag) — faisslite (default) or qdrant
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT a build-time choice: both clients ship in every backend/celery image.
# For the qdrant-backed setup, set all three:
#   KRUTRIM_AGENT_VECTOR_STORE_BACKEND=qdrant
#   COMPOSE_PROFILES=qdrant                      # starts the qdrant container
#   KRUTRIM_AGENT_QDRANT_URL=http://qdrant:6333  # in-compose service address
# Optional qdrant tuning:
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_QDRANT_API_KEY=
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_QDRANT_PREFER_GRPC=false
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_QDRANT_HTTPS=false
# ":memory:" runs an embedded Qdrant (tests / no server); overrides QDRANT_URL.
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_QDRANT_LOCATION=
# Host-published ports for the qdrant service (compose port mapping, bare).
# QDRANT_HTTP_PORT=6343
# QDRANT_GRPC_PORT=6344

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dev mode + Langfuse tracing
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gates local-only tooling (Langfuse below, verbose errors). The dev stack
# (docker-compose.dev.yml) already sets KRUTRIM_AGENT_DEV_MODE=true for you.
# Either name works; KRUTRIM_AGENT_DEV_MODE wins if both are set.
# KRUTRIM_AGENT_DEV_MODE=true
# DEV_MODE=true

# Only traced while dev mode is on, once both keys are set. Bare names (match
# the Langfuse SDK's own).
# LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=
# LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=
# LANGFUSE_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000   # self-hosted; omit for Langfuse Cloud
# LANGFUSE_HOST=https://cloud.langfuse.com  # fallback if LANGFUSE_BASE_URL is unset
# Only read inside docker-compose.yml — repoints the CONTAINERS at a real
# Langfuse URL (they otherwise default to host.docker.internal:3000).
# LANGFUSE_DOCKER_BASE_URL=https://your-langfuse.example.com

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend (apps/web)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Where the BROWSER reaches the backend. Baked in at BUILD time for the Docker
# prod image (Vite convention); read live by `vite dev` / the dev stack. For a
# real deployment set this before `docker compose ... build`.
VITE_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:8000

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# docker-compose — Redis auth (bare names)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave blank for no auth (redis open on its published port). Set both to
# require auth — compose passes REDIS_PASSWORD to redis' --requirepass and
# threads both into KRUTRIM_AGENT_REDIS_URL. Recommended for the prod stack.
# REDIS_USER=default
# REDIS_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CPU / GPU torch build (docker/{backend,celery}.Dockerfile TORCH_BACKEND arg)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# cpu (default, blank == cpu) skips ~5GB of nvidia-* CUDA libs. Read by the
# `builder` stage, so it applies to BOTH dev and prod images. Only set gpu on a
# real CUDA (linux/amd64) host, and uncomment the `deploy:` device-reservation
# block on backend/celery-worker in the compose file.
# TORCH_BACKEND=cpu

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAG format processing stage
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PDF
# PDF_PARSER_ENABLE_OCR_STAGE=false
# PDF_PARSER_ENABLE_ML_STAGE=false

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dev stack only (docker-compose.dev.yml) — file-watch reliability
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# macOS / Windows: native FS events don't reach bind mounts through the Docker
# VM. Flip the relevant one to true if the in-container reloader stops noticing
# edits (costs some idle CPU). Leave false on Linux.
# WATCHFILES_FORCE_POLLING=false   # backend (uvicorn --reload)
# CHOKIDAR_USEPOLLING=false        # frontend (Vite HMR)
# WATCHPACK_POLLING=false          # frontend (Vite HMR)
